{"ref":"BDB, תֹּ֫פֶת³","hw":"תֹּ֫פֶת³","html":"† II. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">תֹּ֫פֶת</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.loc.</strong> in valley of <span dir=\"rtl\">בֶּן־חִנֹּם</span>, S. of Jerusalem <strong>(</strong>etym. doubtful, v. GFM<sup>Ency. Bib. Molech</sup>; RS<sup>Sem. i. 357, 2nd ed. 372, 377</sup> al. think Aramaic, = 9, cf. <a data-ref=\"BDB, שָׁפַת\" href=\"/BDB,_שָׁפַת\", dir=\"rtl\">שׁפת</a><strong>)</strong>;—c. art. <span dir=\"rtl\">הַתּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 23:10\" href=\"/II_Kings.23.10\">2 K 23:10</a> + 5 times, art. om. <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 7:32\" href=\"/Jeremiah.7.32\">Je 7:32</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 19:11\" href=\"/Jeremiah.19.11\">19:11</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 19:12\" href=\"/Jeremiah.19.12\">12</a>;—place of sacrificing children <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 7:31\" href=\"/Jeremiah.7.31\">Je 7:31</a>, cf. v <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 7:32\" href=\"/Jeremiah.7.32\">32a</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 19:6\" href=\"/Jeremiah.19.6\">19:6</a> (cf. v <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 19:5\" href=\"/Jeremiah.19.5\">5</a>), <a data-ref=\"II Kings 23:10\" href=\"/II_Kings.23.10\">2 K 23:10</a>; to become burial place <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 7:32\" href=\"/Jeremiah.7.32\">Je 7:32</a>b; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 19:11\" href=\"/Jeremiah.19.11\">19:11</a>; in sim. of desecrated city v <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 7:12\" href=\"/Jeremiah.7.12\">12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 7:13\" href=\"/Jeremiah.7.13\">13</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(מְקוֹם הַתּ׳)</span>; scene of a prophecy of Jerem., v <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 7:14\" href=\"/Jeremiah.7.14\">14</a>;—Ταφες, Ταφεθ (cf. Lag<sup>BN 78</sup>), 𝔊L <a data-ref=\"II Kings 23:10\" href=\"/II_Kings.23.10\">2 K 23:10</a> Θαφφεθ.—Vid. GFM<sup> l.c.</sup> Salmond<sup>Hast.DB Tophet</sup>.","next":"BDB, תָּפְתֶּה","prev":"BDB, תֹּ֫פֶת²"}